From 1445174ef1ff5794e46b35fe37e0cd6706f72df8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel Mac Builds <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:30:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] deps: make zstandard depend on the site-packages it imports

zstandard's setup.py imports `packaging` at module scope:

  File ".../zstandard/setup.py", line 15, in <module>
    from packaging.version import Version
  ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'packaging'

`packaging` is installed by external_python_site_packages, but
external_zstandard only declared external_python and external_zstd, so a
parallel build is free to run its build step while pip is still
populating site-packages. The deps log shows exactly that interleaving --
pip "Collecting pyproject-metadata / idna / charset-normalizer" lines sit
between zstandard's extract and build steps.

This is a race, not a hard failure, which is why CI saw it
intermittently: run 6 failed here and run 7 passed without the cause ever
being addressed. It reproduced on a 12-job native Intel build.

python_site_packages.cmake deliberately holds numpy, cython and zstandard
out of its pip install because those builds are not reproducible. numpy
and cython both declare external_python_site_packages; zstandard was the
one that did not. This brings it in line, exactly as patch 0002 did for
spirv-tools.
---
 build_files/build_environment/cmake/zstandard.cmake | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/zstandard.cmake b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/zstandard.cmake
index ad757015..06376d44 100644
--- a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/zstandard.cmake
+++ b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/zstandard.cmake
@@ -42,4 +42,15 @@ add_dependencies(
   external_zstandard
   external_python
   external_zstd
+  # zstandard's setup.py does `from packaging.version import Version` at import
+  # time, and `packaging` is installed by external_python_site_packages, not by
+  # external_python. With only external_python declared, a parallel build can
+  # run zstandard's build step while pip is still populating site-packages:
+  #
+  #   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'packaging'
+  #
+  # numpy and cython are held out of the pip install for the same
+  # reproducibility reason noted above, and both already declare this edge.
+  # zstandard was the one that did not.
+  external_python_site_packages
 )
-- 
2.54.0

